meta {
  name: Query (sqld HTTP)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

headers {
  X-Org-Id:
}

body:json {
  {
    "statements": ["SELECT 1"]
  }
}

docs {
  Catch-all reverse proxy onto the caller's sqld namespace (personal by
  default). Anything not matched by the routes above — `/`, `/v2/pipeline`,
  `/v1/...`, and the `/wal_log.*` gRPC services — is forwarded here after
  auth + namespace resolution.

  Namespace selection:
  - No X-Org-Id header -> the caller's personal namespace.
  - X-Org-Id: <org uuid> -> the org's shared namespace, provided the
    caller is a member of a role in that org holding db:query (for
    reads) or db:sync (for the replication/embedded-replica protocol).

  The gateway strips and re-sets Host / x-namespace-bin itself from the
  namespace it resolves server-side — any client-supplied copy of either
  is discarded before forwarding, so it can't be used to reach another
  tenant's namespace.

  Delete the X-Org-Id header entirely (not just leave it blank) to target
  your personal namespace instead of an org.
}
